From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] ui: what closing the VM window does, tested without AppKit

What: a header with no AppKit in it: OmacVM.app's "Closing the window"
(org.omacvm.app closeAction: shutdown, keepRunning, ask; anything else shuts
down) and which value counts (the app's own setting when QEMU runs as the
OmacVM app, else OMACVM_CLOSE_ACTION from the start). Used by
omacvm-cocoa-close.patch (which explains the why).

Why its own file: so the rules are tested without QEMU or a window
(app/runtime/Tests/display/test-close.sh applies this patch to an empty
folder; at build time and in CI).

Upstream: not applicable (OmacVM.app's setting).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-close.c.

diff --git a/ui/omacvm-close.h b/ui/omacvm-close.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ui/omacvm-close.h
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+/*
+ * OmacVM: what closing the VM's window does (#358).
+ *
+ * No AppKit in here, so it is tested on its own
+ * (app/runtime/Tests/display/test-close.c); ui/cocoa.m feeds it.
+ *
+ * OmacVM.app's "Closing the window" (org.omacvm.app closeAction): "shutdown"
+ * (the default) presses the guest's power button and quits when it is off,
+ * "keepRunning" hides the window and the VM goes on (a click on the Dock icon
+ * shows it again; Quit still shuts it down), "ask" asks which. Anything else
+ * shuts down, as before the setting. QEMU started as the OmacVM app reads the
+ * app's own setting when the window closes, so a change while the VM runs
+ * counts; otherwise (a development build, OMACVM_DOCK_SEPARATE) what the app
+ * passed at the start, OMACVM_CLOSE_ACTION.
+ */
+#ifndef OMACVM_CLOSE_H
+#define OMACVM_CLOSE_H
+
+#include <stdbool.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+typedef enum OmacVMClose {
+    OMACVM_CLOSE_SHUTDOWN,
+    OMACVM_CLOSE_KEEP,
+    OMACVM_CLOSE_ASK,
+} OmacVMClose;
+
+static inline OmacVMClose omacvm_close_parse(const char *v)
+{
+    if (v && !strcmp(v, "keepRunning")) {
+        return OMACVM_CLOSE_KEEP;
+    }
+    if (v && !strcmp(v, "ask")) {
+        return OMACVM_CLOSE_ASK;
+    }
+    return OMACVM_CLOSE_SHUTDOWN;
+}
+
+/* app: QEMU runs as the OmacVM app (its own setting, live: NULL = never set). */
+static inline OmacVMClose omacvm_close_pick(bool app, const char *live,
+                                            const char *env)
+{
+    return omacvm_close_parse(app ? live : env);
+}
+
+static inline const char *omacvm_close_name(OmacVMClose c)
+{
+    return c == OMACVM_CLOSE_KEEP ? "keepRunning" :
+           c == OMACVM_CLOSE_ASK ? "ask" : "shutdown";
+}
+
+#endif
